# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign-in — OpenID Connect (OAuth 2.1: authorization code + PKCE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The site is a *public* OAuth client: it ships to the browser, so it holds no
# secret and every one of these is compiled into the bundle. Nothing here is
# confidential — the client id is an identifier, not a credential, which is the
# whole reason PKCE exists.
#
# The provider is authentik (MIT), self-hosted, and it lives in this repository
# at `infra/authentik/`. Bring it up with `docker compose up -d` there; its
# blueprint declares the application, this client and its redirect URIs, so the
# only thing left to do on this side is name it. Read that directory's README
# before changing anything below — both ends have to agree.
#
# In CI these are repository *variables*, set under Settings → Secrets and
# variables → Actions → Variables. Both workflows already read them.

# Discovery root. `/.well-known/openid-configuration` is fetched from it, so
# give the issuer exactly as authentik prints it, trailing slash and all.
PUBLIC_OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:9000/application/o/omnidynamics/

# The client id, matching OMNIDYNAMICS_CLIENT_ID in infra/authentik/.env.
PUBLIC_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=

# Least privilege: ask for the identity, and nothing else. These three are what
# the provider advertises; a fourth would come back `invalid_scope` before any
# login screen appeared. Add one here only when a feature needs it, declare it
# on the provider in the same commit, and say so on /privacy/.
PUBLIC_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email

# ── Going straight to Google, or to a customer's directory ───────────────────
# "Continue with Google" and "Enterprise SSO" are not separate integrations:
# Google and the customer's SAML IdP are federated *behind* authentik, and the
# site gets the same id token whichever way a person came in.
#
# What the button does is skip the screen where authentik asks which one. That
# cannot be a parameter on the authorization request — authentik has no
# `kc_idp_hint` — so it is a flow: one stage, which redirects to the source.
# These name that flow. `infra/authentik/blueprints/omnidynamics.yaml` declares
# the Google one as `google`; leave a line blank and its button is not rendered.
PUBLIC_OIDC_FLOW_GOOGLE=
PUBLIC_OIDC_FLOW_SSO=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Book a demo — Cal.com
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://github.com/calcom/cal.com (AGPL-3.0). Google Meet is not configured
# here, and is not the default: a new event type is booked on Cal Video. To put
# a Meet room on every invitation instead, connect the Google Calendar app in
# Cal.com and set the event type's location to "Google Meet" — a setting on the
# event, with nothing to change in this repository.
#
# team/slug or user/slug of the event type — the path of the booking URL with
# no leading slash, so https://cal.com/s-halim-0296y9/30min is
# `s-halim-0296y9/30min`. That link is the default in `src/lib/auth/config.ts`;
# set this only to point the site at a different event type.
PUBLIC_CAL_LINK=
# Point this at your own instance if you self-host. Defaults to cal.com.
PUBLIC_CAL_ORIGIN=https://cal.com
